---
description: Flutter Logging Guidelines
globs: 
---
{
  "description": "Guidelines for working with Flutter logs in this project",
  "file_patterns": ["**/*.dart"],
  "guidelines": [
    "Log files are stored in the /logs directory at the project root",
    "The primary log file is logs/flutter_run.log, configured in VS Code/Cursor settings",
    Use the run_with_logs.sh script to run the app with logging: ./run_with_logs.sh",
    "You can pass additional Flutter run arguments to the script: ./run_with_logs.sh --flavor dev",
    "Filter logs for cart pricing issues using: tail -f logs/flutter_run.log | grep -E \"CART|💰|⚠️|price|Price\"",
    "Filter by component: grep 'CART_TILE' logs/flutter_run.log",
    "Filter price calculation logs: grep -E '💰|price|CART_DEBUG' logs/flutter_run.log",
    "Filter warnings and errors: grep -E '⚠️|❌' logs/flutter_run.log",
    "Filter specific item data: grep -E 'Item.*menuItemId' logs/flutter_run.log",
    "Extract only log messages with prices: grep -o '.*priceInfo.*' logs/flutter_run.log",
    "Count occurrences of specific log patterns: grep -c 'CART_SUMMARY' logs/flutter_run.log",
    "Search for specific time periods: grep '5:49AM' logs/flutter_run.log",
    "Extract specific log sections: sed -n '/Processing cart/,/processing complete/p' logs/flutter_run.log",
    "Follow logs in real-time with highlighting: tail -f logs/flutter_run.log | grep --color=always -E 'CART|ERROR|WARNING'",
    "Write debug logs using specific prefixes for better filtering: 💰 (price calculations), 🛒 (cart operations), ⚠️ (warnings), ❌ (errors)"
  ]
} 